Z||000008||batboy||12-04-2000||09:57 PM||||Here's what worked for me in the past. Go to a popular expensive jewelry store and pick out a nice looking pair of cheap earrings. That little velvet box makes it seem MUCH more expensive. The lady will think it's MUCH more romantic than fuzzy slippers or a new torque wrench.<P>Another ploy, if you have a sister or other female relative on your shopping list, is to get your lovely g/f to "help" you shop for the sister. Spend several hours shopping, because you "can't" seem to find the "perfect" gift for sis. You'll see what catches your lady friend's eyes, if you watch close enough. Go back alone and buy one of those things that she likes and watch how surprised she is on Christmas. You might even get lucky.||||reg||1
